  "description": "HUKFAY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C81 H74 Cl4 Gd6 N39 O21,16(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.095-4.156 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.51-120.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C81H74Cl4Gd6N39O21·16H2O. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
